Usage:
  nucleus startapp <name> [flags]

Create an app scaffold inside an existing project: model, controller, service, repository, contract, tasks, a server-rendered page and a mountable module, plus the migration for the configured dialect.

Arguments:
  <name>  App name; the model is <Name>, the table and the routes are its plural

Flags:
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file (defaults to <out>/nucleus.yml)
  -data string
    	Repository implementation — quark (default: the Quark ORM over the managed pool, resolved by the same go mod tidy) or sql (database/sql statements for the configured dialect; the model is the same Quark-tagged struct) (default "quark")
  -database string
    	Database alias whose dialect the migration targets (defaults to database_default)
  -dialect string
    	Migration SQL dialect (sqlite|postgresql|mysql|mssql|oracle); defaults to the configured database
  -force
    	Overwrite existing files
  -migrations string
    	Migrations directory (defaults to <out>/migrations)
  -offline
    	Do not touch the network — skip the go mod tidy that resolves Quark and its driver module for the repository (run it yourself before go build)
  -out string
    	Project root output directory (default ".")
  -skip-migration
    	Skip SQL migration scaffold generation

Examples:
  nucleus startapp billing --out .
  nucleus startapp billing --skip-migration
  nucleus startapp billing --data sql   # a database/sql repository instead of Quark
  nucleus startapp billing --offline    # no go mod tidy; run it yourself

The model is a Quark struct (db/pk/quark tags, TableName pinned to the table the migration creates) and the repository runs on the Quark ORM over the framework-managed pool; --data sql renders database/sql statements for the configured dialect over the same model instead. The command ends with go mod tidy, which resolves Quark and its driver module for the engine; --offline skips it and hands it back.
